{
  "_comment": [
    "Calibration store for the Piper MIT compensation stack (see",
    "calibration/CALIBRATION.md). Top-level 'left'/'right' hold the",
    "kp-indexed firmware torque->deflection calibrations for the",
    "kp-offset gravity-compensation path: side -> mit_kp ->",
    "{offset_stiffness, deflection_table}. The follower controllers load",
    "the entry matching their mit_kp at startup and on every mit_kp",
    "change; an uncalibrated kp is rejected with the available values.",
    "Produced by calibration/measure_deflection.py + fit_deflection.py",
    "--update-calibration. k_eff depends on mit_kp, so entries are only",
    "valid at their own kp. Keys under a side MUST stay numeric.",
    "The top-level 'gravity' section holds per-side kp-independent",
    "values with provenance; controllers load them at",
    "startup / on enable when mit_gravity_compensation_calibration_file",
    "is set, falling back to parameter values when a section is absent.",
    "Friction characterization results are stored separately under /data."
  ],
